# Adeni agent rules

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) for the full playbook. These rules always apply.

## Project

Local services marketplace (Lagos, beauty wedge). .NET modular monolith + Next.js web + Expo mobile. Trust-first, SOC 2 from day one.

## Strategy & scope

- [product-strategy.md](../../docs/product-strategy.md) — positioning, revenue, **out of scope**
- [architecture.md](../../docs/architecture.md) — module boundaries, no microservices early
- v1: discovery + booking + portals + Paystack orchestration (no wallet/custody)
- Next sprint: see [sprints.md](../../docs/sprints.md) (Sprint 18 messaging)

## Architecture

`Domain` → `Application` ← `Infrastructure` ← `Api`. Modules via `I*Service` only. `Result<T>` + `.Match()` in controllers. Shared types in `packages/shared`.

## Specs before code

Copy [docs/specs/_template.md](../../docs/specs/_template.md) → `docs/specs/sprint-XX-name.md` before non-trivial features.

## Security (non-negotiable)

- Tenant: EF query filters + `TenantAccessMiddleware` + `X-Tenant-Id`
- PII: `PiiMasker`; never log full phone/email/body
- Admin `/admin/*` → audit logs; MFA when policy enabled
- `DevBusinessAuthMiddleware` only in Development/Testing

## Calibration

Booking → Redis slot locks. Public profile → masked phone. Payments → orchestration only, no custody. **Webhooks → signature + idempotency** (Murphy). **API → `/api/v1/`, auth on mutations, stable error codes** (Murphy). UI → `businessType`/capabilities, not category slugs.

## Workflow

Standing plays in AGENTS.md. Minimal diffs. `dotnet test Adeni.slnx -c Release` before PR.
